[test-suite name=store
  [doc [#
conformance fixtures for cx-stdlib/store (spec/std-lib/store.md §8).

   Each program imports the bundled module via [?lib 'cx-stdlib/store']
   (resolver MUST be quoted) then calls [$store:fn args]. The LAST
   expression is the rendered result. Multi-step programs thread a single
   Store handle through nested [?let [= $s …] …] bindings.

   TWO FIXTURE FAMILIES, split by backend tier (§2.2):

   (A) mem:// FUNCTIONAL MATRIX — the Memory tier (§2.2.1) is pure
   in-process: no filesystem, no network. Per §9 it requires NO host
   capability (D-STORE-1), so these run to completion under the runner's
   empty capability set and assert real content-addressed behavior:
   round-trip, automatic dedup, doc identity (SHA-256 of strict canonical
   bytes, §2.1), not-found / read-only / closed errors, the alias layer
   (§3.9), immutable modify (§3.6), and lossless migrate (§3.10). The
   `golden-hash`-tagged case pins the exact 64-char hex identity recorded
   from the live binary; it equals `cx hash` of the same doc's canonical
   form, confirming the Layer-1 hash surface (spec/misc/bindings.md).

   (B) file:// CAPABILITY-DENY PATHS — a file/local backend touches the
   filesystem, so per §9 `open`/`open-opts` are capability-gated. With no
   active grant in the evaluator (deny-by-default, security.md §2/§4) the
   gated open raises E_CAP_DENIED = cx-err:CXER0271. Only `open` and
   `open-opts` are observable here: every other function takes a
   $store::element that can only be produced by a SUCCESSFUL open, and CX
   errors are values (not propagating exceptions) — a denied open in the
   store-argument position yields an err-node VALUE, which the outer call
   rejects as a bad operand (CXER0100), not a capability denial. The
   per-function file:// deny paths (put/get/list/modify/delete/alias/
   migrate requiring read/write) therefore need a backend whose open
   SUCCEEDS under a partial grant; they are deferred to the
   capability-granted integration harness along with the grant surface.

   STORE-SPECIFIC ERROR CODES on the file:// backend (CXER1100/1101/1120/
   1131/1132; §7) likewise fire only behind a granted open and are
   deferred. The mem:// matrix asserts the store-specific codes it can
   reach without a grant: CXER1110 (read-only), CXER1121 (not-found),
   CXER1130 (closed).

   DEFERRED to the integration suite (flagged, not dropped): cross-backend
   / cross-encoding / cross-binding parity, compression, sharded layout,
   integrity-corruption (CXER1120), auth (CXER1131), rate-limit (CXER1132),
   alias-persistence-across-reopen, concurrent writers, streaming-memory
   bounds, and `query` over CXPath (§3.5) — the path argument is evaluated
   before reaching the call, so query needs CXPath-as-value semantics +
   the full path engine, out of scope for this landing.

   NOTE: no inter-fixture comment blocks appear between cases (a comment
   between sections risks capture into the preceding section payload);
   all explanatory prose lives in this doc header or in tags.
#]]

 [; ── (A) mem:// functional matrix — capability-free (§9, D-STORE-1) ── ]

 [case id=store-rt-001-round-trip-get level=core
  [tags store mem put-doc get-doc round-trip]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/store']
[?let [= $s [$store:open "mem://"]] [= $h [$store:put-doc $s [doc [item "hello"]]]] [$store:get-doc $s $h]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
[doc [item 'hello']]
#]]
 ]

 [case id=store-rt-003-round-trip-quote-bearing-attrs level=core
  [tags store mem put-doc get-doc round-trip attr quoting issue-564]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/store']
[?let [= $s [$store:open "mem://"]] [= $doc [?element "rows" ([?element "row" [?attr "id" "a"] [?attr "title" "has 'quotes' — tricky"]], [?element "row" [?attr "id" "b"] [?attr "title" "has 'quotes' — tricky"]])]] [= $h [$store:put-doc $s $doc]] [$cx:equal [$store:get-doc $s $h] $doc]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
true
#]]
 ]

 [case id=store-rt-004-round-trip-multiword-attr-multiple-docs level=core
  [tags store mem put-doc get-doc round-trip issue-564]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/store']
[?let [= $s [$store:open "mem://"]] [= $e1 [?element "note" [?attr "txt" "two words"]]] [= $e2 [?element "notes" [?element "note" [?attr "id" "n1"]]]] [= $h1 [$store:put-doc $s $e1]] [= $h2 [$store:put-doc $s $e2]] ([$cx:equal [$store:get-doc $s $h1] $e1], [$cx:equal [$store:get-doc $s $h2] $e2])]
#]]
  [out-text [#
(true, true)
#]]
 ]

